settingsForm.querySelector('.settingsGrid').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<article class="panel" data-settings-tab="downloads"><p class="eyebrow">PATH MAPPINGS</p><h2>Download paths</h2><p class="settingHelp">If qBittorrent sees your downloads under a different path than this app does (e.g. qBittorrent runs in its own container with its own mount), add a row below with "qBittorrent path" set to the prefix qBittorrent reports and "Server path" set to the matching prefix on this app's own filesystem, so downloaded files can still be found and processed. Leave the list empty if qBittorrent and this app already agree on paths.</p><div id="mappingList"></div><div class="two"><input id="downloadPrefix" placeholder="qBittorrent path"><input id="localPrefix" placeholder="Server path"></div><button type="button" id="addMapping" class="addRowButton">+ Add mapping</button></article><article class="panel pipelinePanel" data-settings-tab="downloads"><p class="eyebrow">POST-PROCESSING EVENTS</p><h2>Ordered event pipelines</h2><p class="settingHelp">Choose when each step runs: immediately after a successful download, or after finalization. Torrent finalization occurs when qBittorrent confirms removal (including ratio-based removal); successful HTTP downloads run both stages consecutively because they have no separate torrent-removal stage. Steps run once per event in their displayed order.</p><label>Default step timeout (seconds)<input name="pipeline_timeout_seconds" type="number" min="1" step="1" placeholder="30"></label><p class="settingHelp">How long one pipeline step (a shell command or a StashApp call) may run before it's treated as failed - so a hung shell command or an unreachable StashApp can't block post-processing forever. This is only the fallback: set a "Timeout (s)" on an individual step below to override it for just that step, e.g. a script that legitimately takes longer than the rest. Saved with "Save settings" below. Defaults to 30 seconds when left blank.</p><div id="pipelineList" class="stack"></div><div class="two"><button type="button" id="addShellStep">+ Shell / move step</button><button type="button" id="addStashStep">+ StashApp step</button></div><button type="button" id="savePipeline">Save event pipelines</button><p class="pipelineVariables">Shell variables: <code>JAVBEACON_DOWNLOAD_PATH</code>, <code>JAVBEACON_TARGET_PATH</code>, <code>JAVBEACON_RELEASE_ID</code>, <code>JAVBEACON_RELEASE_DB_ID</code>, <code>JAVBEACON_TORRENT_HASH</code>.<br>Set <code>output_path</code> in a shell step to hand the moved destination to later steps in the same event. GraphQL placeholders: <code>{{download_path}}</code>, <code>{{release_id}}</code>, <code>{{release_db_id}}</code>, <code>{{torrent_hash}}</code>.</p></article>`);
settingsForm.querySelector('.settingsGrid').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<article class="panel" data-settings-tab="general"><p class="eyebrow">SCHEDULES & SESSION</p><h2>Background intervals</h2><label>Notification detection<input name="notification_interval" placeholder="15m"></label><label>Provider RSS polling<input name="rss_interval" placeholder="5m"></label><label>Login session lifetime<input name="session_lifetime" placeholder="720h"></label></article><article class="panel coverCachePanel" data-settings-tab="maintenance"><p class="eyebrow">COVER CACHE</p><h2>Historical cover maintenance</h2><label>Cover save path<input name="cover_directory" required placeholder="data/covers"></label><p class="muted">Newly scraped releases are cached automatically in this path. Changing it does not move existing files. Run the job to fill missing covers in the selected location.</p><progress id="coverCacheProgress" max="1" value="0"></progress><p id="coverCacheStatus" class="muted">Loading cover-cache status…</p><button id="cacheAllCovers" type="button">🖼️ Cache all missing covers</button></article>`);settingsForm.querySelector('.settingsGrid').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<article class="panel shortcutsPanel" data-settings-tab="interface"><p class="eyebrow">RELEASE DETAILS</p><h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2><p class="settingHelp">Comma-separate multiple keys for the same action, for example "j, ArrowRight" - shortcuts are alternatives, not a combination. Use a key's own name: a single letter, ArrowLeft, ArrowRight, or Escape. Shortcuts are ignored while a text field has focus, and the same key can't be assigned to two actions.</p><div class="stack"><label>Next release (default: j / ArrowRight)<input data-shortcut="nextItem" placeholder="j, ArrowRight"></label><label>Previous release (default: k / ArrowLeft)<input data-shortcut="prevItem" placeholder="k, ArrowLeft"></label><label>Open Source link (default: s)<input data-shortcut="openSource" placeholder="s"></label><label>Open Sukebei/download-source link (default: d)<input data-shortcut="openDownloadSource" placeholder="d"></label><label>Open Source + download-source links (default: b)<input data-shortcut="openBoth" placeholder="b"></label><label>Search (default: t)<input data-shortcut="searchTorrents" placeholder="t"></label><label>Search & Download (default: g)<input data-shortcut="searchDownload" placeholder="g"></label><label>Toggle Watchlist (default: x)<input data-shortcut="toggleWatchlist" placeholder="x"></label><label>Toggle Notification (default: n)<input data-shortcut="toggleNotify" placeholder="n"></label><label>Toggle Monitored (default: m)<input data-shortcut="toggleMonitor" placeholder="m"></label><label>Update details (default: u)<input data-shortcut="updateDetails" placeholder="u"></label><label>Toggle fullscreen (default: f)<input data-shortcut="fullscreen" placeholder="f"></label><label>Open fullscreen screenshot view (default: p)<input data-shortcut="openScreenshots" placeholder="p"></label><label>Close Release Details (default: Escape)<input data-shortcut="close" placeholder="Escape"></label></div><label class="check"><input id="shortcutForegroundSource" type="checkbox"> Open Source link in foreground</label><label class="check"><input id="shortcutForegroundDownloadSource" type="checkbox"> Open download-source link in foreground</label><label class="check"><input id="shortcutForegroundBoth" type="checkbox"> Open both links in foreground</label><p class="settingHelp">"Foreground" is best-effort: browsers vary in whether a script-opened tab can be forced to the front.</p><button type="button" id="restoreShortcutDefaults">Restore default shortcuts</button></article>`);
settingsForm.querySelector('.settingsGrid').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<article class="panel interfaceScalePanel" data-settings-tab="interface"><p class="eyebrow">READABILITY</p><h2>Interface scale</h2><label>Zoom level<select id="uiZoom"><option value="90">90%</option><option value="100">100%</option><option value="110">110%</option><option value="120">120%</option><option value="130">130%</option><option value="140">140%</option><option value="150">150%</option></select></label><p class="settingHelp">Scales the whole JAVBeacon interface without changing your browser zoom.</p><label>Cover screenshot interval (seconds)<input id="screenshotSlideSeconds" type="number" min="0.1" max="30" step="0.1"></label><p class="settingHelp">How quickly release-card screenshots advance while you hover over a cover. Accepts fractions of a second down to 0.1 (100ms) for a faster slideshow. Stored separately on each browser/device.</p><label>Release Details cover hover delay (seconds)<input id="releaseDetailSlideshowDelaySeconds" type="number" min="0" max="5" step="0.1"></label><p class="settingHelp">How long to hover over the cover on the Release Details page before its screenshot slideshow starts. On iPhone/iPad, tap the center cover area to start and tap again to stop. 0 starts immediately. Stored separately on each browser/device.</p><label>Release Details cover screenshot interval (seconds)<input id="releaseDetailSlideshowSeconds" type="number" min="0.1" max="30" step="0.1"></label><p class="settingHelp">How quickly the Release Details cover screenshots advance once the slideshow starts. Separate from the Release Library interval above and stored per browser/device.</p></article><article class="panel releasePreloadPanel" data-settings-tab="interface"><p class="eyebrow">RELEASE DETAILS</p><h2>Navigation preloading</h2><label>Nearby releases in each direction<input id="releaseDetailPreloadCount" type="number" min="0" step="1"></label><p class="settingHelp">Preloads this many releases before and after the active release so Previous/Next navigation stays immediate. Set to 0 to disable adjacent-release preloading. There is no upper limit.</p><label>Screenshots per nearby release<input id="releaseDetailPreloadScreenshotCount" type="number" min="0" step="1"></label><p class="settingHelp">Preloads this many of each nearby release's screenshots in addition to its details and cover. Set to 0 to preload only release details and covers. There is no upper limit; both values are stored separately on each browser/device.</p></article><article class="panel screenshotBackfillPanel" data-settings-tab="maintenance"><p class="eyebrow">SCREENSHOT CACHE</p><h2>Historical screenshot maintenance</h2><p class="settingHelp">Re-fetches JavLibrary release pages newest-first and caches their preview images separately under <code id="screenshotDirectory">data/screenshots</code>. Completed releases—including releases without screenshots—are remembered and skipped on future runs.</p><label>Backfill job priority (default 75)<input name="job_priority_screenshot_backfill" type="number" min="1" max="999"></label><p class="settingHelp">Priority 1 runs first; 999 runs last. The default lets normal scrape work run ahead of this Cloudflare-sensitive maintenance job.</p><progress id="screenshotBackfillProgress" class="screenshotBackfillProgressBar" max="1" value="0"></progress><p id="screenshotBackfillStatus" class="screenshotBackfillStatusText muted">Loading screenshot status…</p><button id="backfillScreenshots" type="button">🎞️ Backfill missing screenshots</button></article>`);
